/-! # The Wasm 2.0 → Core 3.0 syntax injection

`Types` injects the 2.0 type and immediate syntax, `Instructions` the
instruction syntax, `Modules` the declaration and module syntax, each with a
retraction `ofCore?` that recognises exactly the 2.0 image. Everything below the
instruction level is partial, for the single reason documented in
`ToCore/Instructions.lean`: 2.0's `CVTOP` is untyped.

`ToCore/Modules.lean` also carries the `funcref`/`(ref func)` split of issue
binary-faithful embedding (`Module.toCore` versus `Module.toCoreBinary`). See `Silmaril.Wasm.V2.Validation`.

## The rest of `Silmaril/Wasm/V2/ToCore/` is *above* this file

This module is the **syntax** aggregator only, and it deliberately stops here.
The five other modules of the directory build the semantic halves of the
`2.0 ⊆ 3.0` subset theorem *on top of* it, and each of them opens with
`public import Silmaril.Wasm.V2.ToCore`:

| Module | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `ToCore/Validation.lean` | `ModuleOk.toCore`, `ModuleValid.toCore` — 6-typing is preserved |
| `ToCore/Runtime.lean` | `Store.toCore`, `Config.toCore`, `ToCore.Config.norm`, `ConfigWF`, `Sim` |
| `ToCore/Sim/{Common,Pure,Read,State}.lean` | the per-rule step-simulation lemmas |
| `ToCore/Execution.lean` | `Step.toCore`, `Steps.toCore`, `Diverges.toCore`, `Sim.result` |
| `ToCore/Instantiation.lean` | `allocModule_core`, `prepare_core`, `Instantiate.toCore` |

Adding any of them to the `import` list above would therefore be an import
**cycle**, so the dependency runs the other way and they are reached from
a separate aggregate Wasm import (not included in this package) (or directly), not from here. `ToCore/Instantiation.lean` is
the top of that stack and transitively imports every one of them.
-/
